   "subject": "Parshwanath Capital Ventures Fund | Pre-IPO & Anchor interest – Rediff com India Limited",
   "text": "Dear Milan Soni and Virendra Chaurasia,\n\nI am CA Deep Dalal, Fund Manager of Parshwanath Capital Ventures Fund. I am writing to you as the Book Running Lead Manager to the proposed IPO of Rediff com India Limited, whose Draft Red Herring Prospectus dated November 13, 2026 has been filed with SEBI for listing on the Main Board of BSE and NSE.\n\nABOUT US\nParshwanath Capital Ventures Fund is a SEBI-registered Category III Alternative Investment Fund focused on India's primary markets. We invest through Pre-IPO placements, IPO Anchor Investor books, the QIB portion of IPOs and Qualified Institutional Placements (QIPs), working closely with promoters and merchant bankers through the listing journey.\n\nOUR VIEW ON REDIFF COM INDIA\nRediff com India is a diversified digital platform company with a consumer internet brand and a multi-decade presence in India’s digital ecosystem. We have studied the DRHP closely, and the business and its growth trajectory fit well with our investment focus.\n\nKey financials (restated, ₹ crore unless stated)\n                                    Jun-26*       FY26       FY25       FY24\nRevenue from operations (₹ cr)        58.38     133.59      37.23      36.07\nGrowth (YoY)                              –     258.8%       3.2%          –\nEBITDA (₹ cr)                         39.18      55.48       3.18          –\nEBITDA margin                         67.1%      41.5%       8.5%          –\nNet worth (₹ cr)                     672.86     640.94      82.76     -44.74\nDebt / Equity                         0.59x      0.62x      0.09x     -0.56x\n* Jun-26: interim period, not annualised.\nSource: restated financial information in the DRHP; EBITDA and ratios computed from it.\n\nHOW WE WOULD LIKE TO PARTICIPATE\n  1. Pre-IPO round: Should the Company consider a pre-IPO placement ahead of the RHP, we would be keen to participate.\n  2. Anchor Investor portion: As a SEBI-registered Category III AIF, we qualify as a QIB and would like to be considered for the anchor book.\n  3. QIB portion: We would also look to participate in the QIB portion of the IPO.\n\nFUND PROFILE\nView our fund profile (PDF): https://drive.google.com/file/d/1yQX3TH3nmyqzt6rICyliVYFCP1okKqVv/view?usp=sharing (also attached)\n\nI would be grateful if you could introduce us to the promoters of Rediff com India (Vishal Ajitbhai Mehta) and keep us informed as the pre-IPO and anchor book discussions progress. A short call at your convenience would be much appreciated.\n\nI look forward to hearing from you.\n\nWarm regards,\n\nCA Deep Dalal\nFund Manager, Parshwanath Capital Ventures Fund\nSEBI-registered Category III AIF\nEmail: fundmanager@parshwanath.in\nWhatsApp: +91 83200 52970\nPhone / WhatsApp: +91 70690 06298\nSEBI Reg. No.: IN/AIF3/25-26/2108\n\nThis email is for introduction purposes only and does not constitute an offer, solicitation or commitment to invest. Any investment is subject to the Fund's due diligence, investment committee approval and applicable SEBI regulations. To stop receiving emails from us, reply with “unsubscribe”.",
